README.OSK -- jumble on OS-9/68000ORIG/ is the package as the Microware OS-9 archive carried it for the 6809(c09_jumble): Nick Flor's jumble.c (1987) as ported from Usenet by PeteLyall, his help file, the makefile, and two scripts that keep only thepermutations found in a dictionary -- guess.sh for Unix and guess.go forthe 6809 shell.  The archive's CMDS/jumble is a 6809 module and does notrun here.jumble.c is built for the 68000 exactly as it is; nothing was changed.